TEXT -96 -288 Left 2 ;Problem 2.2 - mass on a spring: M_M = 20 g, k = 1000 N/m -> C_M = 1/k = 1 mm/N, R_M = 0.5 Ns/m.  Left: impedance analogy.  Right: mobility analogy.
TEXT -96 -256 Left 2 ;Top row: driven by a 10 N force.  Bottom row: driven by a 1 m/s velocity.
TEXT -96 -208 Left 2 !.param Mm=20m Cm=1m Rm=0.5
TEXT -96 160 Left 2 ;velocity for 10 N:  I(Vu_A)
TEXT -96 560 Left 2 ;force for 1 m/s:  V(fB)
TEXT 1024 160 Left 2 ;velocity for 10 N:  V(uC)
TEXT 1024 560 Left 2 ;force for 1 m/s:  I(Vf_D)   (L2x has Rser=1u: an ideal L across a V source is a short at DC)
TEXT -96 720 Left 2 !.ac dec 1000 1 1k
TEXT -96 768 Left 2 ;Force drive: the velocity PEAKS at f0 = 35.6 Hz with F/R_M = 20 m/s (26 dB).  Velocity drive: the force DIPS to R_M * 1 m/s = 0.5 N (-6 dB) at the same f0.
